WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.600
The framework begins with an input image and a text prompt specifying the target category to be counted, such as keyboard keys.

2
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:18.310
The image is encoded by a frozen VAE encoder, while the text prompt is processed by a frozen text encoder within the pretrained diffusion model.

3
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:25.050
These representations enter a trainable Denoising U-Net performing a single-step denoising pass to extract intermediate visual features.

4
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:31.430
Multi-layer cross-attention maps are extracted from the U-Net to establish the Representational Regional Coherence loss branch.

5
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:38.550
The fused cross-attention map isolates background regions, combining with ground-truth density locations to build a positive-negative-ambiguous supervision map.

6
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.550
Concurrently, hierarchical multi-scale feature maps from the U-Net decoder enter the Hierarchical Semantic Correction Module.

7
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:51.300
This trainable module progressively refines text-image alignment by fusing visual features across adjacent scales with text embeddings.

8
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.670
Intermediate text-image similarity maps are generated and supervised against the positive-negative-ambiguous map through the coherence loss.

9
00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:04.790
The fully corrected feature representations are then fed into a counter head to estimate the predicted density map.

10
00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:11.910
Finally, the predicted density map is optimized against ground truth annotations with a regression loss, completing end-to-end training.

